{
  "raw": {
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10267": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Music - UT Southern",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Pulaski, TN, United States The department of Humanities and Social Sciences has periodic openings for part-time, adjunct faculty to teach on site or online in the Fine Arts: Music program. The department of Humanities and Social Sciences has periodic openings for part-time, adjunct faculty to teach on site or online in the Fine Arts: Music program. The primary responsibility will be teaching basic to advanced piano classes, individual applied music lessons in piano or other instruments, and upper-level music courses as needed in theory, music tech, composition, and music history. There may be opportunities for piano accompaniment as well. As part of our commitment to academic excellence, we are building a pool of skilled instructors who can contribute to students’ success through engaging and effective teaching. Applications from candidates available to teach on campus will be prioritized. Position Overview: Adjunct instructors in Fine Arts: Music will primarily teach piano-based classes and lessons. There may be opportunities to teach upper-level music courses and to accompany ensembles. Courses may be offered face-to-face or online, though face-to-face is preferred. The principal responsibility of the position is teaching undergraduate students. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without need now or in the future for sponsorship for employment visa status. Qualifications: Master's degree in Music with a specialty in piano, or a related field. Demonstrated piano proficiency. Proven record of quality instruction. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching college-level courses. Experience with learning management systems (LMS) such as Canvas. To apply, please submit 1) a cover letter addressing interest in and qualifications for the role, 2) a CV/resume, and 3) a list of three professional references. For full consideration, candidates should apply electronically through the University of Tennessee Careers site. Candidates who are able to provide on-site accompaniment may be asked to complete a brief audition with the Music Director. Teach courses on-campus or online as assigned. Accompany ensembles and other musical applications, depending on need. Musical applications may include ensemble accompaniment, voice studio, piano lessons, jury examinations, rehearsals, recitals, and university events. Work with the program director to ensure consistent and appropriate student learning. Utilize the University’s learning management system (Canvas) to assess student projects and record grades in a timely manner. Regularly check your email account. Respond to emails/messages in a timely manner. Complete all required reports, such as early grade alerts, midterm grades, and final grades."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10184": {
      "title": "Adjunct Business Professor - UTS",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Pulaski, TN, United States The University is seeking an experienced and student-focused Adjunct Business Faculty member to teach undergraduate courses in business, management, information systems, entrepreneurship, and agricultural business. The successful candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience and a commitment to providing students with engaging, practical, and career-focused learning experiences. The University is seeking an experienced and student-focused Adjunct Business Faculty member to teach undergraduate courses in business, management, information systems, entrepreneurship, and agricultural business. The successful candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience and a commitment to providing students with engaging, practical, and career-focused learning experiences. The ideal candidate will be able to connect business concepts to real-world applications and demonstrate an ability to teach effectively in a traditional or online environment. Candidates with experience in information systems, management, entrepreneurship, agricultural business, leadership, organizational behavior, or related fields are encouraged to apply. The position offers an opportunity to contribute to student success while supporting the University's growing business and agricultural business programs. This is an adjunct, part-time position. Applications will be reviewed on an as-needed basis based on course availability, enrollment, and departmental needs. Submission of an application does not guarantee an immediate assignment or appointment. Because adjunct faculty are hired as instructional needs arise, applicants may not receive a response immediately and should understand that several weeks, months, or potentially longer, may pass before an opportunity becomes available. Qualified applicants may be contacted when a teaching need arises that aligns with their qualifications and experience. The University of Tennessee Southern (UT Southern) is a public university located in Pulaski, Tennessee, strategically positioned within the growing Nashville–Huntsville innovation corridor. As the newest campus in the University of Tennessee System — and the only public four-year institution between Chattanooga and Memphis — UT Southern offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact within a close-knit academic community while benefiting from the resources and reputation of a nationally recognized public university system. With more than 1,000 students, small class sizes, and a highly personalized academic environment, UT Southern combines the feel of a private college with the affordability of a public university. UT Southern’s Firehawks compete in the NAIA Southern States Athletic Conference and include nationally recognized championship programs. Faculty and staff at UT Southern play a direct role in shaping the future of a growing institution committed to academic excellence, student success, workforce development, and regional impact. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without need now or in the future for sponsorship for employment visa status. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Business or related discipline, or a master’s degree with 18 graduate credit hours in the teaching discipline. Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching experience preferred. Professional experience in business, management, information systems, entrepreneurship, agriculture, or a related field is preferred. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate business concepts and engage students in applied, experiential learning. Experience teaching in online, hybrid, or technology-enhanced learning environments preferred. Commitment to student success, timely communication, and providing meaningful feedback to students. Ability to use learning management systems and common instructional technologies effectively. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, program coordinators, and department leadership. Candidates with expertise in agricultural business, entrepreneurship, management information systems, leadership, or organizational behavior are particularly encouraged to apply. Please submit a cover letter that explains your interest in the position and highlights your qualifications for the role, and a current CV as part of your application. Teach assigned undergraduate business courses in accordance with University and department expectations. Prepare and deliver engaging, student-centered instruction in traditional and/or online formats. Maintain regular virtual office hours and provide timely communication and support to students. Evaluate student work and provide timely, constructive feedback that supports student learning and success. Maintain accurate and timely course records, including grades, attendance/participation, and other required documentation. Use the University's learning management system and other instructional technologies effectively. Incorporate current industry practices, real-world applications, and relevant examples into instruction when appropriate. Participate in required faculty meetings, training, professional development, and departmental activities as requested. Communicate regularly with the department head and/or program coordinator regarding course needs, student concerns, and other academic matters. Support the University's commitment to student success, academic quality, and a collaborative learning environment."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10625": {
      "title": "Instructor of Cybersecurity - UT Southern",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Pulaski, TN, United States The University of Tennessee Southern enthusiastically invites applications for the role of a full-time, non-tenure-track Instructor of Cybersecurity. This position combines student-centered teaching, curriculum development, and active service to advance the mission of the University, and the Cybersecurity Program. The Instructor of Cybersecurity will teach courses across cybersecurity and computer science that align with the applicant’s expertise, including areas such as network security, secure software development, systems security, ethical hacking and penetration testing, digital forensics, risk management, cloud security, and introductory programming or computing foundations. The University of Tennessee Southern enthusiastically invites applications for the role of a full-time, non-tenure-track Instructor of Cybersecurity. This position combines student-centered teaching, curriculum development, and active service to advance the mission of the University, and the Cybersecurity Program. The Instructor of Cybersecurity will teach courses across cybersecurity and computer science that align with the applicant’s expertise, including areas such as network security, secure software development, systems security, ethical hacking and penetration testing, digital forensics, risk management, cloud security, and introductory programming or computing foundations. The applicant’s teaching approach must emphasize rigorous, inclusive, and practice-oriented learning. The applicant will design and improve courses with clear, measurable objectives; high expectations; transparent evaluation criteria; and multiple opportunities for students to demonstrate mastery. In cybersecurity and computer science courses, the applicant will use a combination of short lectures, guided demonstrations, hands-on labs, case studies, collaborative problem-solving, simulations, and project-based assessments. Students learn the theory behind secure systems, networks, software, data, and incident response, and how to apply that knowledge responsibly in realistic settings. The applicant will maintain high academic standards while providing structured feedback, accessible learning resources, and support that recognizes the varied backgrounds, experiences, and needs students bring to the classroom. This is an in-person position that begins August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately. For full consideration, please submit your application before 15 December 2026. About the University The University of Tennessee Southern (UT Southern) is a public university located in Pulaski, Tennessee, strategically positioned within the growing Nashville–Huntsville innovation corridor. As the newest campus in the University of Tennessee System — and the only public four-year institution between Chattanooga and Memphis — UT Southern offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact within a close-knit academic community while benefiting from the resources and reputation of a nationally recognized public university system. With more than 1,000 students, small class sizes, and a highly personalized academic environment, UT Southern combines the feel of a private college with the affordability of a public university. UT Southern’s Firehawks compete in the NAIA Southern States Athletic Conference and include nationally recognized championship programs. Faculty and staff at UT Southern play a direct role in shaping the future of a growing institution committed to academic excellence, student success, workforce development, and regional impact. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without need now or in the future for sponsorship for employment visa status. For full consideration, candidates should apply electronically with the following: 1.) a cover letter addressing their interest in and qualifications for the role, 2.) a C.V. and list of at least 3 professional references, and 3.) a Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Applications received before 15 December 2026 will receive full consideration. Required Qualifications: Candidates must possess a strong commitment to teaching, working with college-ready and underprepared students, and serving the university through the cybersecurity program. M.A. in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, or a related discipline A minimum of 1-3 years of teaching at the college level Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and the community Evidence of good character, mature attitude, and professional integrity Expertise in Cybersecurity or in areas of Computer Science related to Cybersecurity Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Cybersecurity or Computer Science 3 or more years of teaching at a college level Expertise in Cybersecurity or in areas of Computer Science related to Cybersecurity Primary duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following: Teach assigned courses in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, and in areas of the candidate’s expertise as needed Teach in-person and online courses Deliver timely feedback on student assignments and projects to promote growth and mastery of learning outcomes Work with learners of all backgrounds Mentor or support students from a wide variety of backgrounds and with differing levels of academic preparedness Employ a variety of teaching methods and styles to effectively engage students and support learning outcomes Establish productive student-oriented projects Assist in the development of new courses and possible revisions of older courses Help develop online cybersecurity and computer science courses Serve on University, Department, and Program committees as assigned Meet weekly office hours and other duties required to meet student and college needs Contribute to the growth and development of the cybersecurity program through recruiting and advising efforts. Contribute to a collegial environment and attend program, department, college, and university meetings to stay connected with university goals and initiatives"
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10624": {
      "title": "Adjunct GIS instructor - UT Southern",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Pulaski, TN, United States The University is seeking an experienced and student-focused Adjunct Geographic Information Systems Faculty member to teach undergraduate courses in GIS. The successful candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience and a commitment to providing students with engaging, practical, and career-focused learning experiences. The University is seeking an experienced and student-focused Adjunct Geographic Information Systems Faculty member to teach undergraduate courses in GIS. The successful candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience and a commitment to providing students with engaging, practical, and career-focused learning experiences. The ideal candidate will be able to connect geographic information systems (GIS) concepts and spatial analysis to real-world applications and demonstrate an ability to teach effectively in a traditional or online environment. Candidates with experience in GIS, geospatial technologies, remote sensing, cartography, spatial data analysis, or related fields are encouraged to apply. The position offers an opportunity to contribute to student success while supporting the University's growing academic programs and preparing students to apply geospatial skills across a variety of professional fields. This is an adjunct, part-time position. Applications will be reviewed on an as-needed basis based on course availability, enrollment, and departmental needs. Submission of an application does not guarantee an immediate assignment or appointment. About the University The University of Tennessee Southern (UT Southern) is a public university located in Pulaski, Tennessee, strategically positioned within the growing Nashville–Huntsville innovation corridor. As the newest campus in the University of Tennessee System — and the only public four-year institution between Chattanooga and Memphis — UT Southern offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact within a close-knit academic community while benefiting from the resources and reputation of a nationally recognized public university system. With more than 1,000 students, small class sizes, and a highly personalized academic environment, UT Southern combines the feel of a private college with the affordability of a public university. UT Southern’s Firehawks compete in the NAIA Southern States Athletic Conference and include nationally recognized championship programs. Faculty and staff at UT Southern play a direct role in shaping the future of a growing institution committed to academic excellence, student success, workforce development, and regional impact. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without need now or in the future for sponsorship for employment visa status. Please submit a cover letter that explains your interest in the position and highlights your qualifications for the role, and a current CV as part of your application. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Geography, GIScience, Geospacial Analytics, Geo-Informatics or related discipline, or a Master’s degree with 18 graduate credit hours in the teaching discipline. Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching experience preferred. Professional experience GIS or a related field is preferred. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate concepts and engage students in applied, experiential learning. Experience teaching in online, hybrid, or technology-enhanced learning environments preferred. Commitment to student success, timely communication, and providing meaningful feedback to students. Ability to use learning management systems and common instructional technologies effectively. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, program coordinators, and department leadership. Candidates with expertise in agricultural business, entrepreneurship, management information systems, leadership, or organizational behavior are particularly encouraged to apply. Teach assigned undergraduate GIS courses in accordance with the University and department expectations. Prepare and deliver engaging, student-centered instruction in traditional and/or online formats. Maintain regular virtual office hours and provide timely communication and support to students. Evaluate student work and provide timely, constructive feedback that supports student learning and success. Maintain accurate and timely course records, including grades, attendance/participation, and other required documentation. Use the University's learning management system and other instructional technologies effectively. Incorporate current industry practices, real-world applications, and relevant examples into instruction when appropriate. Participate in required faculty meetings, training, professional development, and departmental activities as requested. Communicate regularly with the department head and/or program coordinator regarding course needs, student concerns, and other academic matters. Support the University's commitment to student success, academic quality, and a collaborative learning environment."
    }
